    "body": "## Overview\n\n`GET /v1/responses/{response_id}?starting_after=N` accepted any integer\nfor `starting_after`. Negative values flowed into\n`start_index = starting_after + 1` and indexed the event `deque` from\nthe right (Python negative indexing), producing either an HTTP 500 or a\nsilently corrupted replay. This PR bounds the query parameter and clamps\nthe computed index.\n\n## Claims\n\n- `starting_after` below -1 is rejected with 422 by FastAPI\n  (`Query(ge=-1)`).\n- The replayed stream always starts from a non-negative deque index; the\n  `response.completed` terminal event is always reachable.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Before the fix, two failure modes were reproducible at logic level\n  against the exact generator code (`serving.py`, `retrieve_responses`\n  streaming path):\n  - `starting_after=-5` with a 3-event buffer:\n    `IndexError: deque index out of range` → HTTP 500.\n  - `starting_after=-2` with a 3-event buffer: replay began from the\n    LAST buffered event (`deque[-1]`), emitted events out of order, and\n    never delivered `response.completed` — the stream hung.\n- After the fix: `ge=-1` rejects lower values with 422, and\n  `max(0, starting_after + 1)` guarantees a valid start index even for\n  `-1` (replay from the beginning, matching the \"no value\" behavior).\n\n## Details\n\n`starting_after + 1` is intended as \"resume after the given event\nindex\". For negative inputs Python's deque indexing wraps from the tail,\nwhich breaks both the ordering invariant of SSE replay and the\ntermination condition of the streaming loop (the loop exits only when it\nyields an event of type `response.completed`; a tail-starting replay\nskips it).\n\nThe clamp and the schema bound are redundant by design: the schema bound\ngives clients a clean 422, the clamp protects the generator against any\nfuture caller path.\n\nThis PR was created with AI assistance; the submitter has reviewed and\ntakes responsibility for every line.\n",
